==French==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|fr}} {{term|laisser|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|fro|fr}} {{term|lesser|lang=fro}}, {{term|lessier|lang=fro}}, {{term|laissier||to let, let go, leave|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la|fr}} {{m|la|laxō|laxō, laxāre|to relax, loosen}}; partly from or influenced by {{etyl|goh|fr}} {{m|goh|lāzzan}}, {{term|lāzan||to let, let go, leave||tr={{etyl|de|-}} {{term|lassen|lang=de}}|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|fr}} {{m|gem-pro|*lētaną||to let, leave, leave alone}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|fr}} {{m|ine-pro|*lēy-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*lēi-d-||to leave, let}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|sc=Latinx|lǣtan||to allow, let go, leave, rent}}, {{etyl|got|-}} {{term|𐌻𐌴𐍄𐌰𐌽||tr=letan|to release, forgive|lang=got|sc=Goth}}. Conflated also with {{etyl|fro|-}} {{term|laiier||to leave, abandon, allow|lang=fro}} (compare {{etyl|pro|-}} {{term|laihar|lang=pro}}, {{term|laiar||lang=pro}}, Old Northern {{etyl|it|-}} {{term|lagare||lang=it}}), also of {{etyl|gem|-}} origin, from {{etyl|got|-}} {{term|𐌻𐌰𐌲𐌾𐌰𐌽||tr=lagjan|to lay, let lie, leave|lang=got|sc=Goth}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|fr}} {{m|gem-pro|*lagjaną||to lay}}. More at {{l|en|let}}, {{l|en|lay}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Fr-laisser.ogg|audio|lang=fr}}
* {{IPA|/lɛse/|lang=fr}}

===Verb===
{{fr-verb}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=fr}} to [[leave]], to [[leave]] behind
#: '''''Laissez''' le pistolet sur la table''
#:: ''Leave the gun on the table''
# {{context|transitive|lang=fr}} to [[forget]], to [[leave]] alone
# {{context|transitive|lang=fr}} to [[leave]] with, to [[give]]
# {{context|transitive|lang=fr}} to [[let]], to [[allow]]
# {{context|reflexive|se laisser|lang=fr}} to [[allow]] oneself, to [[let]] oneself

